  "implemented": [
    "Finite written conditional local destinations split and join complete borrowed facts; exact signed constant array offsets retain tracked targets.",
    "Independent definite ARC strong aliases keep loans alive through source rebinding. Forward/reverse/transitive aliases, conditional expiry and lexical lifetime boundaries are checked; last-owner loss still expires.",
    "Raw native-frame task-group callbacks use typed adoption and failure disposal; explicit group callable spawning owns closures through frame teardown. Typed native task-join declarations work in both source languages.",
    "Named nontrivial C++ keypath values use native copy/move initialization, materialized operand snapshots and destruction. Record-field writeback, lvalue/temporary subscript assignment and throwing copy/setter cleanup pass source/PCH and sanitizers.",
    "Native allocator/deallocator, size/alignment, nonnull, format/format-argument and Linux calling-convention contracts retain typed payloads, export dependencies, replay identity and provider calling ABI.",
    "Unnamed C++ member records under complete template owners preserve lexical nominal origins, exact closed/partial arguments and member-template overload/argument identities. Partial owners, nested templates, identical sibling layouts, relocation, AST import and source-free ABI are exercised."
  ],
  "scope": [
    "The native backend and runtime/header inputs remain unchanged across the full normal/ASan/TSan feature matrices. Later unnamed-record publication changes affect the frontend facade and package fixtures, checked by the final frontend/package reports.",
    "Instrumented runtime service archives and GNUstep runtimes are reused unchanged. No SDK archive was rebuilt.",
    "Focused package reports bind the checker source before the full-fixture expected owner sets gained NativeDeclarationAttributes::Projected. Only check_cpp_metadata changed; check_factory_metadata and compiler/runtime/fixture inputs are unchanged. Final full-fixture reports bind the corrected checker.",
    "Clang retains the allocator/deallocator annotation with its existing ignored-form warning. Publication binds that AST contract; no additional deallocation-mismatch analyzer is claimed.",
    "Public signatures exposing unnamed template member types are rejected pending a broader projection/ABI contract. Managed-union, borrowed/resource and undefined nullable keypath result-policy boundaries remain explicit.",
    "Full-fixture executions are three smoke configurations, not its complete cross-product or final-binary SDK qualification. Earlier failed and intermediate reports are retained."
  ],
  "accepted_sdk_version": "2.62.0",
  "sdk_rebuilt": false,
  "profile_conformance_claimed": false,
  "native_linux_aarch64_qualified": false,
  "remaining": [
    "Remaining public dependent/unnamed-type and lookup projections; unmodeled attributes and general standard-library publication/implementations.",
    "General indirect/union/alias and borrowed-result precision, mutable/reference/generic/lazy callable analysis, global/foreign/MRC and exceptional ownership effects.",
    "Remaining abstract spawn/group forms, isolation/Sendable crossings and complete Strict Concurrency enforcement.",
    "Dependent/effectful/isolated and borrowed/resource keypaths; undefined nullable nonnull/scalar/aggregate result policy and Part 8 resource-union boundary.",
    "Remaining specified language/library/metaprogramming/foreign interop, required diagnostics and complete Core/Strict/Strict Concurrency/Strict System profiles.",
    "Native Linux AArch64 implementation/qualification and coordinated post-2.62 SDK delivery."
  ]
